  "TM0099": {
    "source": "Plano de ubicacion, Portal Sur - JFK Coop Financiera, version noviembre de 2024.",
    "why": "THREE platforms drawn LEVEL and identical: the same rectangle three times, 325 to 822, stacked 108 apart, each with the planting behind it as a round-capped band of the same width — which is why the platform itself is drawn with SQUARE ends and the green with round ones, and why a platform drawn the way Portal 80 draws its own came out 26px too long at each end and swallowed the green. One pedestrian tunnel crosses all three at the same point and lands on the Acceso peatonal block below them. The bays are not cut into a bar here: each is a short bar in the ROUTE OWN COLOUR set beside its name, out on the page under the platform. And the furniture is printed the other way round from the other two portals — a grey glyph on a PALE tile rather than a white one knocked out of black. The bay marks carry the colour the SHEET prints, not the catalog route colour: this plan inks its alimentadores one blue, its zonales one green and its troncal bay orange, and a plano is a snapshot of the operator printing rather than a live view of the catalog.",
